# MANDATORY: Slint build / run

After changes to `crates/noviewlog-slint/`, `crates/noviewlog-core/` (when used
by Slint), or Slint packaging scripts, build or run Slint yourself. Do **not**
ask the user to rebuild.

## What the user runs

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `bash scripts/run-slint.sh` | `cargo run --profile release-dev` + run `noviewlog-slint` (Linux) |
| `scripts/run-slint-windows.ps1` | Same daily profile on Windows (imports MSVC env) |
| `cargo build --profile release-dev -p noviewlog-slint` | Daily optimized binary (no fat LTO) |
| `cargo build --release -p noviewlog-slint` | Publish profile (fat LTO) |
| `bash scripts/publish-slint-windows.sh` | Windows MSVC → `dist/noviewlog-slint-win-x64/NoViewLog.exe` |

## Required commands (Linux)

```bash
bash scripts/run-slint.sh
# or
cargo build --profile release-dev -p noviewlog-slint
```

## Required commands (Windows)

```powershell
.\scripts\run-slint-windows.ps1
# or (after MSVC env is active)
cargo build --profile release-dev -p noviewlog-slint
```

Do **not** use `run-slint.sh` or `.deps` fontconfig helpers on Windows.

`run-slint.sh` MUST use `--profile release-dev` (`opt-level = 3`, no fat LTO).
A debug `cargo run` pegs ~100% CPU on PTY flood even when optimized is fine —
do not treat debug as the product path. Fat `--release` (LTO + CGU=1) is for
publish only; it disables incremental and makes every small edit a full relink.

Do **not** set `RUSTFLAGS=-L…/.deps/lib` in the run script or the shell: it
changes the rustc fingerprint of every crate and forces a full rebuild when
the script and a plain `cargo` disagree. Link search lives in
`crates/noviewlog-slint/build.rs`; pkg-config paths live in `.cargo/config.toml`.

## Windows release folder

Run on a Windows host with the MSVC Rust toolchain (not Linux cross):

```bash
bash scripts/publish-slint-windows.sh
```

## Agent obligations

1. Run the appropriate command(s) yourself — do **not** tell the user to rebuild.
2. Do **not** claim Slint work is done until the build (or publish on Windows) succeeds when those surfaces changed.
3. Linux fontconfig helper: `scripts/setup-slint-deps.sh` (used by `run-slint.sh`) — do not port to Windows.
4. PTY / Follow / Viewport / HOST_TICK changes: a green compile is **not**
   acceptance. Run the daily GUI (`release-dev`) and measure `cat` per
   [terminal-flood-verify.mdc](terminal-flood-verify.mdc).
